WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:08.153
When Pollyanna awoke the next morning, it was a beautiful day.

2
00:00:08.154 --> 00:00:14.415
Through an open window, she spotted Aunt Polly and Tom in the garden.

3
00:00:14.416 --> 00:00:18.247
Pollyanna ran outside and threw her arms around her aunt.

4
00:00:18.248 --> 00:00:24.475
"Aunt Polly! Aunt Polly! Today I'm glad just to be alive!"

5
00:00:24.476 --> 00:00:26.986
"Is this how you usually say good morning?"

6
00:00:26.987 --> 00:00:32.226
Aunt Polly scolded, releasing herself from Pollyanna's grip.

7
00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:41.379
"Only to people I love!" Pollyanna danced around Aunt Polly, who tried to frown but failed.

8
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:46.230
"You may finish trimming those roses," Aunt Polly said to Tom.

9
00:00:46.231 --> 00:00:49.666
Then she hurried into the house.

10
00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:55.145
"You're so like your mother, little miss," said Tom, picking up his clippers.

11
00:00:55.146 --> 00:00:59.184
"I knew her when she was your age."

12
00:00:59.185 --> 00:01:06.209
Pollyanna gasped. "You did? Oh, please, tell me all about her!"

13
00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:10.645
Tom had barely begun to speak when a bell sounded from the house.

14
00:01:10.646 --> 00:01:14.410
The next minute Nancy flew out the back door.

15
00:01:14.411 --> 00:01:18.701
"Hurry up!" Nancy pulled Pollyanna toward the house.

16
00:01:18.702 --> 00:01:21.121
"That bell means it's time to eat.

17
00:01:21.122 --> 00:01:27.717
If you don't come quickly, it'll be hard to find anything to be glad about."

18
00:01:27.718 --> 00:01:33.206
At the breakfast table, Aunt Polly and Pollyanna ate in silence.

19
00:01:33.207 --> 00:01:37.785
As Nancy brought in more muffins, Aunt Polly noticed two flies.

20
00:01:37.786 --> 00:01:42.108
"Nancy, where did those flies come from?"

21
00:01:42.109 --> 00:01:44.227
"I don't know, ma'am."

22
00:01:44.228 --> 00:01:48.174
"They're probably my flies," Pollyanna said cheerfully.

23
00:01:48.175 --> 00:01:54.737
"A whole bunch of them were having a wonderful time in my room this morning."

24
00:01:54.738 --> 00:01:59.487
Struggling not to laugh, Nancy left the room with the muffins.

25
00:01:59.488 --> 00:02:02.696
"Nancy!" Aunt Polly called.

26
00:02:02.697 --> 00:02:07.497
Nancy returned with a serious look on her face and the muffins.

27
00:02:07.498 --> 00:02:14.001
"You may put down the muffins and close the windows in Miss Pollyanna's room," Aunt Polly said.

28
00:02:14.002 --> 00:02:18.340
"Pollyanna, keep those windows closed until we have screens.

29
00:02:18.341 --> 00:02:24.553
Flies spread all kinds of diseases."

30
00:02:24.554 --> 00:02:29.878
After breakfast Aunt Polly handed Pollyanna a pamphlet on flies.

31
00:02:29.879 --> 00:02:35.473
Pollyanna's eyes lit up when she saw an enlarged illustration of a fly's head.

32
00:02:35.474 --> 00:02:41.449
"Thank you!" she exclaimed, skipping from the room.

33
00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:47.141
Awhile later Aunt Polly went up to Pollyanna's room.

34
00:02:47.142 --> 00:02:52.453
"Oh, Aunt Polly, I never read anything so interesting in my life!"

35
00:02:52.454 --> 00:02:55.272
Pollyanna said with great enthusiasm.

36
00:02:55.273 --> 00:03:00.519
"I'm so glad you gave me that article. I had no idea flies—"

37
00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:06.727
"That's enough," said Aunt Polly, who'd meant the pamphlet as punishment for opening the windows.

38
00:03:06.728 --> 00:03:13.407
"I'd like to examine your clothes to see if they're suitable for living here with me."

39
00:03:13.408 --> 00:03:16.700
With great reluctance, Pollyanna opened her closet.

40
00:03:16.701 --> 00:03:22.826
"I'm afraid you'll think they're awful.

41
00:03:22.827 --> 00:03:26.868
You see, they all came from the donation box at church.

42
00:03:26.869 --> 00:03:30.768
Did you ever get your clothes from a donation box?"

43
00:03:30.769 --> 00:03:35.614
Seeing Aunt Polly's shocked face, Pollyanna quickly corrected herself.

44
00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:41.573
"Of course not. You're rich—though in this room it's easy for me to forget you're rich.

45
00:03:41.574 --> 00:03:44.840
It was hard to play the game with my clothes, but Fath—"

46
00:03:44.841 --> 00:03:49.979
Pollyanna stopped when she remembered Aunt Polly didn't want to hear about her father.

47
00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:58.972
Aunt Polly abruptly started examining Pollyanna's clothes. "I assume you went to school?"

48
00:03:58.973 --> 00:04:04.548
"Yes, and sometimes Fath—I mean, I was taught at home too."

49
00:04:04.549 --> 00:04:06.847
Aunt Polly looked stern.

50
00:04:06.848 --> 00:04:12.002
"You'll start school in the fall, but in the meantime, you'll be on a strict schedule.

51
00:04:12.003 --> 00:04:15.458
Every day before breakfast, you'll tidy this room.

52
00:04:15.459 --> 00:04:19.379
At nine o'clock you'll read aloud to me for half an hour.

53
00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:25.793
On Wednesdays and Saturdays, you'll spend the rest of the morning in the kitchen with Nancy, learning to cook.

54
00:04:25.794 --> 00:04:28.549
On the other mornings, I'll teach you to sew.

55
00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:32.351
You'll spend your afternoons practicing the piano."

56
00:04:32.352 --> 00:04:39.143
Pollyanna squirmed. "I don't really like playing the piano."

57
00:04:39.144 --> 00:04:44.426
"I'm sure that's true, but you will take piano lessons here."

58
00:04:44.427 --> 00:04:52.927
Pollyanna sighed deeply. "With all these activities, you haven't left me time to just live.

59
00:04:52.928 --> 00:04:58.817
You know, to climb hills and talk to Tom and explore the town."

60
00:04:58.818 --> 00:05:02.999
Now it was Aunt Polly's turn to sigh.

61
00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:08.494
"I'm doing my duty by ensuring that you have proper care and instruction.

62
00:05:08.495 --> 00:05:11.584
You must do your duty too.

63
00:05:11.585 --> 00:05:15.730
Don't waste these opportunities and don't be ungrateful.

64
00:05:15.731 --> 00:05:19.911
There will be some time for play."

65
00:05:19.912 --> 00:05:23.895
Aunt Polly was halfway down the stairs when Pollyanna called after her.

66
00:05:23.896 --> 00:05:26.732
"What did you think of my clothes?"

67
00:05:26.733 --> 00:05:29.232
"We'll go shopping this afternoon.

68
00:05:29.233 --> 00:05:38.819
If I let you appear in public in those clothes, I wouldn't be doing my duty!"

